  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SL&amp;L Programme Strategy Development, Reflection and Review</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This operational budget is to support the design and development of the new Programme Strategy for Sierra Leone and Liberia using the Integral Ecology Programme Model (IEPM). 
In line with &#x2018;Our Common Home&#x2019;, CAFOD has renewed its commitment to work in the most poor and vulnerable contexts in both countries by developing and adopting the Integral Ecology Programme Model (IEPM). The IEPM ensures that CAFOD works in the most disadvantaged areas, meeting the needs of the extreme poor, most vulnerable and marginalized, and the challenging environmental and climatic issues facing them.
There are seven steps in this strategy development process to be completed but the first  operational budget is focusing on the delivery of the first two steps: Situational Scoping and Programme Approaches (consultants to be hired to help facilitate the delivery of the work) and also subsequent Annual Reflection and Discernment processes.</narrative>
  </description>
